findings.message:
url_match_conn() runs url_match_auth_ntlm() before the newly added url_match_auth_nego():

  if(!url_match_auth_ntlm(conn, m))
    return FALSE;          /* <-- returns before nego check ever runs */
  else if(m->force_reuse)
    return TRUE;           /* <-- also returns before nego check */

  if(!url_match_auth_nego(conn, m))
    ...

url_match_auth_ntlm() returns TRUE only when neither want_ntlm_http nor want_proxy_ntlm_http is set (or when it already set force_reuse). Consequently, whenever the transfer wants NTLM (e.g. CURLOPT_HTTPAUTH = CURLAUTH_ANY / --anyauth, which includes both CURLAUTH_NTLM and CURLAUTH_NEGOTIATE, or an explicit NTLM|NEGOTIATE mask), url_match_auth_nego() is never executed and the new Negotiate credential/state binding is not applied at all.

That by itself would only mean 'no new protection', but the NTLM helper also records a fallback candidate and returns FALSE:

  if(m->want_ntlm_http) {
    if(Curl_timestrcmp(m->needle->user, conn->user) ||
       Curl_timestrcmp(m->needle->passwd, conn->passwd)) {
      if(conn->http_ntlm_state == NTLMSTATE_NONE)
        m->found = conn;      /* lib/url.c:1137-1138 */
      return FALSE;
    }
  }

Curl_cpool_find() (lib/conncache.c:598-636) always invokes the done callback url_match_result(), which attaches match->found even though every url_match_conn() call returned FALSE.

Concrete path:
1. Transfer A: `curl --anyauth -u alice:pw1 https://host/` completes SPNEGO/Negotiate on connection C. C now has conn->user="alice", conn->http_negotiate_state == GSS_AUTHSUCC and conn->http_ntlm_state == NTLMSTATE_NONE (NTLM was never used).
2. Transfer B: `curl --anyauth -u bob:pw2 https://host/` on the same handle/share. want_ntlm_http is TRUE, so url_match_auth_ntlm() is entered, the credentials differ, http_ntlm_state == NTLMSTATE_NONE, so m->found = C and it returns FALSE. url_match_conn() returns FALSE at lib/url.c:1286 and url_match_auth_nego() (which would have rejected C because m->needle->user != conn->user) is never reached.
3. url_match_result() attaches C to transfer B.

Result: Bob's request is sent over a connection the server considers authenticated as Alice (Negotiate is connection-bound), i.e. the exact credential-confusion/authentication-bypass this PR claims to fix remains reachable in the most common configuration that actually enables Negotiate (--anyauth). Note HTTP has PROTOPT_CREDSPERREQUEST, so the generic credential comparison in url_match_auth() (lib/url.c:1046) does not apply and cannot catch this.

